THE BRIEFING -- print it to the user BEFORE calling the tool.

Q-30 — The to-do list user guide says restoring the database always rewinds the whole application and never brings back a single task. The restore runbook's default option copies one table, or chosen rows, on its own. Which one is right?
  wstrzymuje: COH-spec_sync-6
  A: Keep partial restores; fix the guide  ← the recommendation
      Skutek: The guide and the runbook's opening lines say that one list, or chosen tasks, can be brought back on their own
  B: Whole-database restores only
      Skutek: The runbook stops offering to copy one table or chosen rows, and restores always rewind everything

Q-31 — The to-do list user guide was written into the change record because the author could not write to docs/, where this project keeps user guides. Where should it live?
  wstrzymuje: COH-spec_sync-7
  A: Move it to docs/ with the other guide  ← the recommendation
      Skutek: It becomes docs/user-guide-todo-list.md with a row in docs/README.md, and the conventions name the person using a screen as a docs/ reader
  B: Leave it in the change record
      Skutek: The guide stays as history of this change only, and the to-do list screen has no user guide under docs/

